Retry a spliced Anthropic stream instead of killing the run.

`@ai-sdk/anthropic` fails a stream with

    AI_InvalidResponseDataError: Received message_start for message "msg_B"
    while message "msg_A" is still open.

when a second `message_start` arrives before the first message closed.  That
happens when an intermediary — a gateway, or Anthropic's own edge — loses its
upstream connection mid-generation, retries, and concatenates the retried
generation's SSE events onto the *same* HTTP response body.  The response then
carries generation A truncated mid `content_block` (no `content_block_stop`)
followed by a complete generation B.

The error is not a bug, it is the guard vercel/ai added in #18332 / #18402 to
fix #18331.  Before it, both generations were merged into one recorded step;
the signed thinking blocks of a generation Anthropic never completed were then
replayed on the next request, which Anthropic rejects with a *non-retryable*
400 "`thinking` or `redacted_thinking` blocks in the latest assistant message
cannot be modified".  Failing loudly is the correct behaviour.

What is missing is recovery.  The request itself was always well-formed, so
resending it is all that is needed, but `retryable()` never matches the
message and the run dies.  Observed ~20 times over three days on
`anthropic/claude-opus-5` over direct OAuth with no gateway in the path.

Two changes:

  * packages/opencode/src/session/retry.ts — add the message to
    `RETRYABLE_MESSAGE_PATTERNS`.  `fromError()` classifies
    `InvalidResponseDataError` through `case e instanceof Error` into
    `NamedError.Unknown`, so `retryable()` reaches its non-API tail and decides
    purely on the message text.  `streamInput.messages` is built once in
    `prompt.ts` before `handle.process()`, so a retry resends the original
    request — the corrupt partial is never fed back in.

  * packages/opencode/src/session/processor.ts — drop the parts a failed
    attempt already persisted before retrying.  This is required, not
    cosmetic: the splice usually severs the stream *after* the thinking block
    closed, so generation A leaves behind a complete, signed reasoning part.
    `toModelMessagesEffect()` replays reasoning parts with their
    `providerMetadata` and filters nothing, so a recovered stream would hand
    Anthropic A's orphaned signature on the following turn and reproduce the
    exact 400 that #18331 was about, one turn later.

    Parts are identified by attempt rather than by content because an
    abandoned generation is indistinguishable from a good one on inspection —
    both can be complete and signed.  `PartID` is `prt_` plus a fixed-width
    monotonic prefix, so a marker taken at the start of an attempt orders
    strictly below every part that attempt goes on to write.  The marker is
    reset at the top of each `process()` call: it is per-attempt, and the tool
    loop calls `process()` once per step, so a step's first attempt must not
    sweep up the previous step's successful parts.

    This also cleans up after the mid-stream errors opencode already retries
    (`ECONNRESET`, `ResponseStreamError`), which leave the same debris today.

Applies to 1.18.29.  Drop this patch once upstream retries the spliced-stream
error itself.

